<title>FINLAND: UPM, M-Serla rise on Stora Q1.</title>
<headline>UPM, M-Serla rise on Stora Q1.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish forestry groups UPM-Kymmene and Metsa-Serla rose sharply on Thursday after Swedish Stora reported first-quarter results above analysts' expectations, brokers said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's Stora's result,&quot; one broker said when asked what was boosting UPM.</p>
<p>At 1520/1220 GMT, UPM-Kymmene traded at a seven-week high 118.50 markka, up 3.50 markka or more than three percent, in fairly active 44 million markka volume on an thin bourse.</p>
<p>Metsa-Serla B was up 1.20 markka at 38, but trade was quiet.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 235</p>
</text>
